T1  - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder in women with subclinical hypothyroidism
T3  - 38th Annual Meeting of the European Thyroid Association, ETA 2014. Santiago de Compostela Spain.
A1  - Petrova M.
A1  - Hristozov K.
A1  - Momova G.
A1  - Shishkov R.
A2  - Pacini F.
Y1  - 2014//
N2  - Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder/ADHD/ usual begins in childhood but excessive activity, impulsivity and academic failure are a hallmark of social behaviour of the person throughout his/her entire life. Test of clinicbased voluntary patients monitor less expressed impulsivity and hyperactivity of women in comparison with those of men. Among the wide spectrum of psychic syndromes ADHD is a manifestation of thyroid deficiency. Molecular markers for ADHD are still under research, but the prevailing opinion is that the diagnosis is clinical. <ovid:br/>Aim(s): To investigate the frequency of ADHD in women and to assess the influence of subclinical hypothyroidism/SH/ on ADHD. <ovid:br/>Method(s): 2591 patients have been examined in the Clinic of Psychiatry and Medical Psychology during 2010. 35 of them responded to the diagnostic criteria of ADHD according to DSM-IV (verbal and non verbal tests). Functional test of the thyroid include TSH, FT4, FT3/RIA/, US/7, 5 MHz/. Controul group-20 healthy nonpregnant women. <ovid:br/>Result(s): From all 2591 subjects 35 have ADHD/frequency 1, 35%/. 22 patients have increased TSH and they are subjects of psychlogical and endocrinological tests. The clinical manifestations of the 22 tested subjcects are grouped as follows: A/ Predominant hyperactivity and impulsivity: n = 7 / femals/, age 22.45; score from psychic tests =110; TSH 6.77 mU/l; FT4 20.54 pmol/l; index of correlation between IQ and TSH- /r = -0.24/; B /Predominant inattention n =11/, age 23.15; score from psychic tests =114; TSH 6.98 mU/l; FT4 23.14 pmol/l; index of correlation between IQ and TSH- /r = - 0.31/; C/ Combined symptoms n = 4, age 21.18; score 98, TSH 5.98 mU/l; FT4 18.32 pmol/l; index of correlation between IQ and TTH- /r = -0.09/; <ovid:br/>Conclusion(s): The frequency of ADHD among women with SH is 1.35%. Attention tests monitor prevailing impairment in women with SH.
