T1  - An adult woman with ADHD: Substance use disorder and gender bias misleading the diagnosis
T3  - ADHD bij een volwassen vrouw: Middelenafhankelijkheid en genderbias als misleidende factoren in de diagnostiek
A1  - Alexandre M.
A1  - Van Duyse A.
Y1  - 2013//
N2  - ADHD ("attention deficit hyperactivity disorder") is now commonly diagnosed among adults, although clinicians still tend to ignore the diagnosis when co-existing disorders, such as substance use disorders, may mask the core symptoms of ADHD. In this case report of a 22-year-old Caucasian woman, it is assumed that the female gender represents an additional pitfall in the diagnosis of ADHD. This manuscript therefore aims to kindle the interest among professionals to develop adequate skills to recognize ADHD.
